//? Title: Rabin-Karp: actual rolling windows and exact collision rejection
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
String matching must locate every occurrence, including overlaps, without
mistaking a hash collision for equality. Rabin-Karp rolls a modular polynomial
hash across fixed-length windows and verifies candidate bytes exactly. Actual
native hashes replace the old report-local hash illustration. The original text
abababbb and pattern aba remain, with explicit forced-collision, empty-pattern
and embedded-NUL controls.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For unsigned bytes \(c_i\), Horner hashing gives
\(H=\sum_{i=0}^{m-1}c_i b^{m-1-i}\bmod p\). Set \(w=b^{m-1}\bmod p\). Sliding by
one byte gives
$$ H^+=\{(H-c_{out}w)\,b+c_{in}\}\bmod p. $$
\alttext(Remove the outgoing leading byte contribution, multiply by the base and append the incoming byte.)
Reducing after each widened product preserves this polynomial identity. Hash
equality is only a candidate: the producer compares unsigned bytes until
mismatch or full equality. Exact verification proves that every reported offset
is a match, even with a deliberately tiny composite modulus. Overlaps follow by
visiting every start offset.

With rare collisions, preprocessing plus one rolling update per window gives
typical linear work. Repeated candidates can require \(O(nm)\) verification; the
fixed deterministic hash has no unconditional adversary-resistant collision
bound. The empty pattern convention yields all n+1 positions and performs no
hashing.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rabin_karp_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    a::RabinKarpOptions o;
    o.modulus = 2;
    o.base = 1;
    auto t = a::rabin_karp_trace("ca", "a", o);
    const auto &s = t.windows[0];
    std::print("\n| actual offset | window hash | candidate | exact match | compared bytes |\n| ---: | ---: " "| --- | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.windows)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.start, e.hash, e.candidate,
                   e.matched, e.compared_bytes);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first hash / pattern hash\n{} / {}", s.hash,
                       t.pattern_hash));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual candidate / byte decision\n{} / {}", s.candidate,
                       s.matched));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual accepted byte offsets\n{}", t.matches));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/rabin_karp_tiny.svg");
}
```
